# 2. Product Definition

## 2.1 Product vision

Seedance Forge is a **cinematic pre-production operating environment**.

It is not primarily an image-generation application. Its core responsibility is to transform narrative and visual intent into a structured production system in which:

- story beats become scenes;
- scenes become shots;
- shots inherit visual continuity;
- characters become locked visual identities;
- environments become locked architectural/atmospheric references;
- camera composition becomes explicit;
- prompts are compiled from structured production data;
- animatics and production documents derive from the same project state.

## 2.2 Core principle

**One Project State → Multiple Production Views**

Storyboard, Script, Character, Environment, Depth, Prompt Studio, Animatic, Bible, Inspector and Export must never maintain conflicting copies of project truth.

All views read from and write to the same normalized project state.

## 2.3 Primary user

The primary user is a filmmaker, director, art director, storyboard artist, pre-production designer, cinematographer, or AI-assisted visual production designer.

---

# 3. Product Goals

## 3.1 Primary goals

- Provide a unified cinematic pre-production workspace.
- Maintain visual identity and continuity across shots.
- Convert source documents into structured production entities.
- Allow manual and AI-assisted refinement.
- Make camera language explicit and reusable.
- Generate prompts from production facts rather than isolated text.
- Produce an editable animatic from storyboard timing.
- Produce a Visual Production Bible.
- Produce set-ready printable documentation.
- Support local/offline workflows.
- Persist projects in a portable `.seedance` format.

## 3.2 Non-goals

The application is not intended to be:

- a full nonlinear video editor;
- a final VFX compositor;
- a final 3D DCC;
- a final audio workstation;
- an image-generation backend itself.

AI generation providers are integrations. Seedance Forge remains the orchestration and continuity layer.

---

# 4. Design Principles

## 4.1 Source of truth

The uploaded/source material is the authoritative basis for extracted narrative facts.

AI must not silently invent production facts.

Unknown or ambiguous information must remain explicitly unknown, inferred, or unresolved.

## 4.2 Continuity over artistic improvisation

The system must prioritize:

1. identity consistency;
2. environment consistency;
3. camera consistency;
4. narrative continuity;
5. production usability.

## 4.3 Structured data over free-form duplication

Whenever information can be represented as a structured field, it should not be duplicated in unrelated text fields.

## 4.4 Reversible editing

Major project mutations must support undo/redo.

## 4.5 Local-first operation

Core authoring, navigation, editing, saving, loading, prompt compilation, timeline calculation and mock AI operation must work without a remote service.

## 4.6 Production outputs derive from project state

PDF, CSV, Bible, animatic and prompt exports must be generated from the same canonical state.

