# 31. Responsive / Interaction Requirements

The supplied implementation emphasizes:

- pointer capture;
- dynamic viewport scaling;
- resize handling;
- event delegation;
- preserving input focus;
- avoiding unintended canvas gestures.

Rules:

1. Canvas pan ignores interactive controls.
2. Board drag must not initiate canvas pan.
3. Input fields must stop propagation where necessary.
4. Modal interactions must be isolated from the canvas.
5. Resize must preserve world coordinates.
6. Zoom must remain cursor-centered.

---

# 32. Visual Design System

The current approved visual direction must be preserved.

## 32.1 Style

- dark cinematic workspace;
- glass/translucent panels;
- subtle glow for focus;
- technical metadata;
- restrained motion;
- clear hierarchy;
- production-tool aesthetic.

## 32.2 Avoid

- generic SaaS styling;
- excessive rounded cards;
- decorative gradients without semantic purpose;
- excessive centered layouts;
- visual noise;
- replacing functional metadata with decorative UI.

## 32.3 Typography

Typography must prioritize:

- compact metadata;
- readable production text;
- clear hierarchy;
- screenplay readability.

---

# 33. Visual Frame Renderer

The current prototype uses procedural SVG placeholders.

This should remain supported as a lightweight fallback.

## 33.1 Inputs

- shot type;
- aspect ratio;
- palette;
- horizon;
- subject scale;
- depth;
- letterbox state.

## 33.2 Renderer

The SVG may include:

- sky/radial gradient;
- horizon;
- sun/moon;
- subject silhouette;
- rule-of-thirds guides;
- anamorphic bars.

## 33.3 Purpose

The renderer is a **production planning visualization**, not a final image generator.

---

# 34. Continuity Validation

The system should detect:

- shot without Character Lock where one is expected;
- shot without Env Lock where one is expected;
- inconsistent character references;
- missing environment reference;
- invalid depth assignment;
- missing prompt fields;
- contradictory camera metadata;
- frames with invalid duration.

Validation must be visible without preventing legitimate exploratory work.

