# 36. Error Handling

Errors must be classified as:

- validation;
- persistence;
- parser;
- AI provider;
- export;
- integration.

User-facing errors must explain:

1. what failed;
2. whether project data was affected;
3. what the user can do next.

AI failures must never corrupt existing locks or canonical data.

---

# 37. Performance Requirements

The application must remain responsive with:

- dozens of boards;
- hundreds of frames;
- large script documents;
- multiple characters;
- multiple environments;
- long timelines.

Performance principles:

- avoid full application rerenders for pointer movement;
- use memoization/selectors;
- isolate board state;
- use requestAnimationFrame for playback;
- debounce expensive parsing;
- avoid persistence on every pointer move;
- virtualize large lists where needed.

