# 39. Acceptance Criteria

The implementation is considered functionally complete when:

### Canvas

- [ ] pan works without accidental board movement;
- [ ] zoom is cursor-centered;
- [ ] board world positions remain stable.

### Storyboard

- [ ] scenes can contain multiple frames;
- [ ] frames can be added/edited/deleted;
- [ ] frames can be reordered;
- [ ] frames can move between scenes.

### Script

- [ ] Fountain can be edited;
- [ ] Fountain can be previewed;
- [ ] scene headings and dialogue are parsed.

### Character

- [ ] character entities persist;
- [ ] turnaround references persist;
- [ ] Prompt Lock persists;
- [ ] Prompt Lock can be generated through AI.

### Environment

- [ ] SOAC fields persist;
- [ ] references persist;
- [ ] Env Lock persists;
- [ ] Env Lock can be generated through AI.

### Camera

- [ ] all nine shot types are available;
- [ ] lens is editable;
- [ ] movement is editable;
- [ ] depth layers are editable.

### Prompt Studio

- [ ] selected shot is represented;
- [ ] character/environment locks are included;
- [ ] prompt compiles deterministically;
- [ ] platform-specific output is supported;
- [ ] clipboard works.

### AI

- [ ] Mock provider works offline;
- [ ] Ollama can discover available models;
