# 42. Architectural Invariants

The following rules are mandatory and should be treated as non-negotiable implementation invariants.

### INV-001 — Single Source of Truth

All production views derive from canonical project state.

### INV-002 — Character Continuity

A Character Prompt Lock is the authoritative visual identity descriptor once approved.

### INV-003 — Environment Continuity

An Environment Env Lock is the authoritative environment descriptor once approved.

### INV-004 — Shot Context

A shot prompt must be capable of referencing character, environment and camera context.

### INV-005 — Timeline Consistency

Animatic timing must derive from frame durations.

### INV-006 — Export Consistency

Exports must derive from canonical project state.

### INV-007 — Reversibility

Destructive project mutations must be undoable.

### INV-008 — Source Traceability

Imported source material must remain traceable.

### INV-009 — Local Operation

Core project authoring must not depend on a remote AI service.

### INV-010 — Visual Continuity

UI evolution must preserve the approved Seedance Forge visual language.

